// WebGLEngine/tools/ship/takeRankingValidity-selfcheck.mjs -- UNNUMBERED (the version is chosen at ship time)
//
// Run: node tools/ship/takeRankingValidity-selfcheck.mjs      (about 20 s)
//
// THE GATE OF tools/ship/takeRankingValidity.mjs (+ takeRankingValidityCmd.mjs): the audit of "does the held-out score rank the searches", registered in brain/RANKING_VALIDITY_WIP.md before any code. The searches are the REAL 24 of the two training files; the audit files here are SYNTHETIC (built by this gate with the lead of each search chosen), except the one-dive real flights of section 7. No search is flown on the registered block.
//   1  THE CONSTANTS   the block, the files, the family order, the six champion digests (against the earlier audit files that recorded them), alpha, the tie tolerance, the Monte Carlo's seed and draws.
//   2  THE SEARCHES    the 24 real searches in order; their held-out leads (unpriced for plain-priced); eligibility (16: 2, 3, 2, 3, 4, 2); the six champions; synthetic training lines for the rule (none eligible, ties to the lower k).
//   3  THE STATISTICS  sgn; sOf by hand; the exact within-family test against an independent enumeration of the whole product of arrangements (6,912 for the real eligible set) and against the counts printed in the registration (S >= 8 is p 0.0483, S >= 6 is 0.1212, S = 14 is 1 in 3,456); the Monte Carlo against an enumeration of 5,040 arrangements and its generator against the published mulberry32; the OLS line; the reading at the edge of alpha.
//   4  THE AUDIT FILE  readAudit refuses by its words; leadsOf; earlierLeads (synthetic and the real earlier audit files); championRows.
//   5  THE CHECKS      all six pass on a good audit, word for word; each fails by its words.
//   6  THE REPORT      word for word at the three readings (RANKS, BACKWARDS, DOES NOT RANK), the failed-check shape, the label of a block that is not the registered one, Q2e with and without the earlier leads.
//   7  THE COMMAND     the arguments and their refusals, `fly` (resume, the stale-file refusal, workers, one arm), `report`, and the real thing: one real dive flown through the library, through `--one` in a child process, and through `runChild`.
// NOT CHECKED, said plainly: the 25 arms on the registered block (not flown until the read); that a synthetic audit's numbers mean anything (they exercise the arithmetic and the words).
//
// SABOTAGE LOG: filled in below when the sweep is run.
"use strict";
import fs from "node:fs";
import os from "node:os";
import path from "node:path";
import { spawnSync } from "node:child_process";
import { fileURLToPath } from "node:url";
import * as X from "./takeRankingValidity.mjs";
import * as D from "./trainDecisionCircuit.mjs";
